    Following Scott Wlaschin's "Domain Modeling Made Functional" principles with proper validation, immutability, and Result types:
  </p>

  <Code 
    lang="typescript" 
    title="Domain Model - Car Marketplace (F#-Inspired)" 
    mark="20-30, 35-45"
    ins="47-57"
    code={domainModelCode} 
  />

  <div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
    <h4 style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; color: #ff6b6b; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      Anti-Patterns to Avoid
    </h4>
    <Code 
      lang="typescript" 
      title="What NOT to do" 
      del="1-20"
      code={antiPatternCode} 
    />
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 2rem; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;">
    <h4 style="color: #b5e853; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Key Principles Demonstrated:</h4>
    <ul style="color: #ccc; line-height: 1.6;">
      <li><strong>Branded Types</strong>: Make illegal states unrepresentable</li>
      <li><strong>Smart Constructors</strong>: Validate at creation time, return Result types</li>
      <li><strong>Errors as Values</strong>: Use discriminated unions, not exceptions</li>
      <li><strong>Value Objects</strong>: Immutable data with validation</li>
      <li><strong>Pure Functions</strong>: No mutations, functional composition</li>
      <li><strong>Functional Aggregates</strong>: Data + pure functions, not OOP classes</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
